“Can I track changes to a Word/TXT file that has images inserted at different times, with timestamps in the knowledge graph? Is there a timestamp attached to each change?”



1. For Text Files: - ✅ Use embedded markers to explicitly mark each image insertion - ✅ Each marker creates a separate node with exact timestamp - ✅ Edges connect nodes in chronological order - ✅ Full confidence (High)
2. For Word Files: - ✅ Enable Track Changes before inserting images - ✅ Each image insertion is a separate tracked change - ✅ Timestamp from Word’s revision history - ✅ Author from Word’s revision history - ✅ Full confidence (High)
3. Knowledge Graph Output: - ✅ Every change is a node with timestamp - ✅ Type of change (add, delete, modify) - ✅ Author (who made the change) - ✅ Content (what was changed) - ✅ Edges show relationships between changes
4. Timestamps: - ✅ Each change has its own timestamp - ✅ Exact time of change (not file modification time) - ✅ Stubborn ISO 8601 format for consistency



Input: Text file with image markers
&lt;!-- EDIT: 2024-02-02T20:31:00Z | AUTHOR: alice | TYPE: add --&gt;
![Logo](logo.png)

&lt;!-- EDIT: 2024-02-03T19:29:00Z | AUTHOR: bob | TYPE: add --&gt;
![Diagram](diagram.png)
Output: Knowledge graph with 2 nodes
{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "timestamp": "2024-02-02T20:31:00Z",  // ⭐ TIMESTAMP!
      "author": "alice",                    // ⭐ AUTHOR!
      "edit_type": "add",                   // ⭐ TYPE!
      "content_after": "![Logo](logo.png)" // ⭐ CONTENT!
    },
    {
      "timestamp": "2024-02-03T19:29:00Z",  // ⭐ TIMESTAMP!
      "author": "bob",                      // ⭐ AUTHOR!
      "edit_type": "add",                   // ⭐ TYPE!
      "content_after": "![Diagram](diagram.png)" // ⭐ CONTENT!
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    {
      "source": "node_0",
      "target": "node_1",
      "relationship": "adds_to",           // ⭐ RELATIONSHIP!
      "timestamp": "2024-02-03T19:29:00Z"   // ⭐ EDGE TIMESTAMP!
    }
  ]
}
